msgid "Off"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30025"
msgid "2x"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30026"
msgid "4x"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30027"
msgid "8x"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30028"
msgid "Allows you to use mouse inputs even when User 1's device type isn't set to 'RetroKeyboard/Mouse'."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30029"
msgid "Stamp scuff marks on walls where hitscan shots land. Off by default, matching ZDoom mods that do not request bullet decals; enable for the classic wall-chip marks."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30030"
msgid "Give GLDEFS point lights a vertical light pool on walls (brightest at the light's height, fading up and down) instead of a single level per wall column. Off by default; the per-band shading is noticeably heavier on tall, close, heavily-lit walls."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30031"
msgid "Scans parent folders for IWADs. NOTE: You need to disable this if you want to run SIGIL."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30032"
msgid "Enables haptic feedback when using a rumble-equipped gamepad."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30033"
msgid "Load WAD data by memory-mapping the file instead of reading it fully into RAM. Lowers memory use and speeds up loading of large WADs, since only the lumps actually used are paged in. Falls back to a normal read for archives, if mapping fails, or on builds without memory-mapping support. Leave disabled to perform all WAD file I/O up front at load time."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30034"
msgid "Sets the deadzone of the gamepad analog sticks when the input device type is set to 'Gamepad Modern'."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30035"
msgid "Forces a demo-compatibility level. 'Default' uses the engine's automatic choice. Set 'MBF21' to play MBF21 WADs that require complevel 21."
msgstr ""

